\chapter{Validation, Stress Testing, and Conclusions}

\section{Shock-Wave and Caustic Stress Protocol}
The engine is stress-tested under hypersonic inflow Mach numbers
$M_\infty \approx 5.2$, extreme temperature spikes, and
$\max\|\nabla\rho\| > 10^4$. Caustic formation in the optical domain is
handled via symplectic integration and dynamic interpolation grids.

\section{Formal Validation Summary}
The ROESEE architecture satisfies:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Eulerian--Lagrangian energy conservation in the PDE kernel.
    \item Symplectic phase-space invariance in the Hamiltonian ray-tracing system.
    \item Maximal diffusion and confusion in the cryptographic transformation.
\end{itemize}
Together, these properties establish a physically anchored, mathematically
rigorous optical-encryption engine.

